<title>GERMANY: GRUNDIG CEO RESIGNS WITH IMMEDIATE EFFECT.</title>
<headline>GRUNDIG CEO RESIGNS WITH IMMEDIATE EFFECT.</headline>
<dateline>FUERTH, Germany 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Troubled German home electronics maker Grundig AG said on Monday former CEO Pieter van der Wal quit, leaving his office six weeks sooner than expected.</p>
<p>&quot;I had told the company I was willing to remain in service for two months. But today I must recognise that the basis for the association has fallen away,&quot; van der Wal wrote in a letter to supervisory board chief Christian Schwarz-Schilling.</p>
</text>
